spans.s:
urvī́, f. earth;
 du. heaven and earth;
 🞄pl. w. ṣaṣ, the six terrestrial spaces (four 🞄quarters, above & below;
 sometimes explained 🞄as heaven & earth, day & night, water & plants).

urvī-tala, n. surface of the earth, 🞄earth;
 -dhara, m. mountain;
 -pati, m. king;
 🞄-bhuj, m. id.;
 -bhiṛt, m. mountain;
 -ruha, 🞄a. sprung from the earth;
 m. tree.

ūr-vá, m. reservoir;
 fold, cattle-pen;
 🞄N. of a saint.
